From 203d7147d61ff0646ff9113d0355d147379822d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: b1air <dimazzzzz342@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 08:07:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Add workspace_animation slide

Switching workspaces can slide both sideways, the new one in from the
side it lies on, as Hyprland and GNOME do, instead of swayfx's fade.
Each workspace slides from wherever it is drawn: mid-slide, or held
aside by a swipe (swipe_offset/swipe_peek, used by the swipe patch).
Floating windows move with their workspace; while it slides they are
placed without the per-window move animation, which would pull them
back on every frame.

workspace_animation fade|slide, default fade.
